  "worked_solution": "First, we write the expression as a difference of squares:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{s}^{2}}{25}-\\frac{1}{81}={(\\frac{s}{5})}^{2}-{(\\frac{1}{9})}^{2}\n$$\n\nThen, we factor the expression using the difference of squares formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{s}{5})}^{2}-{(\\frac{1}{9})}^{2}=(\\frac{s}{5}+\\frac{1}{9})(\\frac{s}{5}-\\frac{1}{9}) & .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
